{
  "abstract": "For every n at least eleven there is an n-denomination coin system in which greedy change is optimal for every amount in the first three prefixes and the full system, but not in any intervening prefix. This refutes the general prohibition in Conjecture 5.2(1) at each length 3r+1 for r at least four. At every length 3r+2 for r at least four there is a counterexample to the exhaustiveness claim in 5.2(3), outside both families D and G.",
